# ReBeep reference screen: help2-2op, vga
# help page 2 of 2 over synth 2-OP: patch FACTORY\BRASS "BRASS" with unsaved edits (* shown), routing FM, operator 2 Attack Rate in focus, chip OPL3, keys held C4 G4, message none
glyphs
 Bank ◄ FACTORY  ►   Patch ◄ BRASS    ► *  2 of 4        Variant 2-OP  Octave 4 
┌ ┌─ Help · What the controls mean ───────────────────────────────── 2 of 2 ─┐─┐
│ │                                                                          │ │
│ │ Attack Rate           Rise time: 1 is 2.8 s, 14 is 0.35 ms, 15 instant.  │ │
│ │ Decay Rate            Fall to Sustain Level: 1 is 39 s, 15 is 2.4 ms.    │ │
├ │ Sustain Level         Level held while the key is down; 3 dB a step.     │ ┤
│►│ Release Rate          Fade after key up: 1 is 39 s, 15 is 2.4 ms.        │ │
│ │ Output Level          Volume, 0.75 dB a step. On a modulator: more tone. │ │
│ │ Key Scale Level       High notes get quieter: 0, 1.5, 3 or 6 dB/octave.  │ │
│ │ Frequency Multiplier  Pitch x½ to x15: x1 is the note, x2 an octave up.  │ │
│ │ Waveform              The wave's shape: 4 on OPL2, 8 on OPL3.            │ │
│ │ Tremolo               Volume wobbles, 1 or 4.8 dB (set for the chip).    │ │
│ │ Vibrato               Pitch wobbles, 7 or 14 cents (set for the chip).   │ │
│ │ Sustained             On: holds at Sustain Level until the key is up.    │ │
│ │ Key Scale Rate        The envelope runs faster on higher notes.          │ │
│ │ Connection            How operators feed each other: carriers are heard, │ │
│ │                       modulators shape them. 2-OP has 2 choices, 4-OP 4. │ │
│ │ Feedback              Operator 1 feeds its own output back into itself.  │ │
├ │                       0 is a pure tone, 7 is buzzy and noisy.            │ ┤
│ │                                                                          │ │
│ │ ▐2▌ carrier: you hear it    ▐1▌ modulator: shapes a carrier's tone       │ │
│ │ Sustain Level and Output Level: bigger means louder.                     │ │
│ └─────────────────────────── ◄ ► page   F1 or Esc closes ──────────────────┘ │
└──                                                                            ┘
